From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: dts: ingenic: thingino-t20: describe the Helix VPU

The generic T20 board copied the T31 AVPU node even though the T20 has
the older Helix encoder at the same address and INTC line.  The node
never bound, because the AVPU driver is T31-only, and it left the real
VPU without a device.

Replace it with the T20 VPU node, using the VPU clock added to the CGU
driver.  No T20 board references the old `avpu` label.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/thingino-t20.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/thingino-t20.dts
@@ -26,15 +26,13 @@
 		reg = <0x0 0x8000000>;
 	};
 
-	avpu: avpu@13200000 {
-		compatible = "t31,avpu";
+	vpu: vpu@13200000 {
+		compatible = "ingenic,t20-vpu";
 		reg = <0x13200000 0x100000>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
 		interrupts = <62>;
-		clocks = <&cgu T31_CLK_EL150>,
-			 <&cgu T31_CLK_AHB1>,
-			 <&cgu T31_CLK_VPLL>;
-		clock-names = "el150", "ahb1", "vpll";
+		clocks = <&cgu T31_CLK_VPU>;
+		clock-names = "vpu";
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 
